---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/ui/PageHero.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="How Mod Labs collects, uses and keeps information when you book a service, request a quote or send a device in.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy" intro="The plain-language version of how I handle your information." compact />
  <section class="section-y pt-10 sm:pt-14">
    <div class="container-x">
      <div class="prose-lab">
        <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> September 2026</p>

        <h2>What I collect</h2>
        <p>
          When you use the booking or quote forms, I collect what you enter: your name, email, phone number (optional), how you'll get
          the device to me, the services or request type you pick, your message and any photos you attach. That's it. There are no
          accounts on this site.
        </p>

        <h2>How the forms work</h2>
        <p>
          Form submissions are processed on Cloudflare, which hosts this site. To block spam, the forms use
          <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong>, which may check basic browser and device signals to tell people from bots. Your request
          is then emailed to me through <strong>Resend</strong>, an email delivery service, along with any photos you attached. Photos
          are resized in your browser before they're sent, which also drops their location data.
        </p>

        <h2>Why I use it</h2>
        <p>
          Only to reply to your request, give you a quote, schedule the work and coordinate drop-off or shipping. I don't sell your
          personal information, and I don't use it for advertising.
        </p>

        <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Requests are kept as long as needed for the job and for reasonable business records, unless the law requires longer. You can
          ask me to delete your information at any time.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies & analytics</h2>
        <p>
          This site doesn't use advertising or tracking cookies. Cloudflare may process technical data (like IP addresses) to deliver
          the site securely and prevent abuse.
        </p>

        <h2>Devices & data on hardware</h2>
        <p>
          Consoles and other devices may contain your accounts, saves and personal files. Please back up anything important before
          handing a device over. Typical mod installs don't require wiping storage, and I don't go through your data.
        </p>

        <h2>Questions or requests</h2>
        <p>
          To ask about or delete your information, send a message through the <a href="/quote">quote form</a> and pick "General
          question".
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
